# orders

Order management.

A gRPC service with a REST mapping (grpc-gateway), built on
[kitchen](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/dungnh3/kitchen): `server` (gRPC +
REST + probes + graceful shutdown), `errs` and `i18n` (one error model for
gRPC and HTTP), `auth` (JWT/JWKS), `ratelimit`, `log` and `otelx`, with
PostgreSQL through `pg` (pgx) and sqlc, and goose migrations through `migrate`.

## Run

```bash
make db-up        # local Postgres in Docker
make run          # gRPC on :10000, REST on :8080, auth disabled
make test         # unit tests and an integration test of the whole service
make lint
```

Try it:

```bash
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/items -d '{"title":"first"}'
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/items
```

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `proto/orders/v1/` | The API: messages, validation rules (protovalidate) and REST mapping |
| `gen/` | Generated by `make generate` from `proto/` (committed); OpenAPI in `gen/openapi/` |
| `cmd/server/` | `main`: logging, configuration, the `migrate` command |
| `internal/app/` | Wiring: telemetry, database, auth, rate limits, server; integration test |
| `internal/config/` | Configuration from environment variables |
| `internal/service/` | The API implementation |
| `internal/store/` | The `Store` interface and its implementations (`memstore`, `pgstore`) |
| `internal/store/pgstore/queries.sql` | SQL queries; `make generate` turns them into `sqlcdb` (committed) |
| `migrations/` | goose migrations, embedded in the binary |

## Change the API

1. Edit `proto/orders/v1/*.proto` (validation rules go in the proto file).
2. Add a migration in `migrations/` and queries in `internal/store/pgstore/queries.sql`.
3. Run `make generate`, then implement the new methods in `internal/service`.

Return `errs` errors from methods (`errs.ErrNotFound`, `errs.BadRequest(...)`,
`errs.New(codes.FailedPrecondition, "REASON", ...)`); they become the same
`google.rpc.Status` on gRPC and the AIP-193 JSON error on REST, localized from
`Accept-Language`. Any other error is logged and the client sees a generic
internal error.

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Deployment name; `production` refuses unsafe settings |
| `GRPC_ADDR` | `:10000` | gRPC listen address |
| `HTTP_ADDR` | `:8080` | REST and `/livez`, `/readyz` |
| `ADMIN_ADDR` | | Admin port, for example `:9090`: `/readyz` with details, `/version`, `/metrics` (Prometheus), `/debug/pprof/`. Keep it private |
| `GRPC_REFLECTION` | `false` | gRPC server reflection (authenticated like other methods) |
| `SHUTDOWN_DELAY` | `5s` | Time to keep serving after readiness turns off |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Total graceful shutdown budget |
| `TRUSTED_PROXIES` | | Comma-separated CIDRs of the proxies in front of the service (client IP for rate limits) |
| `ERROR_DOMAIN` | `orders` | `ErrorInfo.domain` of API errors |
| `DB_URL` | (required) | `postgres://` URL; TLS is required unless it sets `sslmode` |
| `DB_MAX_CONNS` | max(4, CPUs) | Pool size |
| `DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Per-statement timeout |
| `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START` | `false` | Apply pending migrations before serving |
| `AUTH_ISSUER` | (required) | JWT issuer (`iss`) |
| `AUTH_JWKS_URL` | (required) | Issuer key set; https only (http for localhost) |
| `AUTH_AUDIENCE` | (required) | This service's audience (`aud`) |
| `AUTH_TOKEN_TYPES` | | Accepted JWT `typ` values, for example `at+jwt` |
| `AUTH_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn auth off; refused when `APP_ENV=production` |
| `RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn rate limits off |
| `RATE_LIMIT_DRY_RUN` | `false` | Count and log, never reject |
| `RATE_LIMIT_EXEMPT` | | Comma-separated `user:<id>`, `ip:<address>` or `ip:<CIDR>` |
| `LOG_LEVEL`, `LOG_FORMAT`, `LOG_SCHEMA`, `LOG_OUTPUT` | `info`, `json`, detected, stdout | See `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/log` |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and other `OTEL_*` | | Traces (and metrics, logs) are exported over OTLP only when an endpoint is set |

Authentication is fail-closed: without `AUTH_*` (or an explicit
`AUTH_DISABLED=true` outside production) the service does not start, and an
unreachable JWKS stops startup too. Only the gRPC health service is public.
Restrict methods by scope with `auth.RequireScopes` in `internal/app`.

Every package logs through `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/log` (`main` calls
`log.Setup`), and `.golangci.yml` keeps it that way: it denies `log/slog` and
the libraries behind every canonical kitchen package (raw Redis, SQL and HTTP
clients, `http.Server`, `status.New`, OTel SDK setup, ...). Use `redisx`,
`httpx`, `cache`, `lease`, `pubsub`, `timex` and friends instead.

Rate limits use per-instance memory. To share them between instances, pass a
Redis store (`github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/ratelimit/redis`) as
`ratelimit.Config.Store`.

## Migrations

```bash
server migrate up        # apply pending migrations (run as a deploy step / init container)
server migrate down      # roll back the last one
server migrate status
```

A Postgres advisory lock serializes concurrent runs. `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START=true`
runs `up` at startup instead, which suits local development.

## Events

To publish events reliably, write them in the same transaction as the data
with the transactional outbox `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/pubsub/outbox/pgx`
(add its `Schema()` to a migration) and relay them to Pub/Sub, Kafka or SQS
with the `pubsub` adapters.

## Deploy

`make docker` builds a static binary into a distroless image that runs as
nonroot. For private modules, pass `--build-arg GOPRIVATE=...` and
`--secret id=netrc,src=$HOME/.netrc`; the credentials never land in a layer.
Point the Kubernetes probes at `/livez` and `/readyz` on the HTTP port (or the
admin port).
